{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And his father refused and said: I know, etc.</b> His saying <b>and he refused</b> — because he wanted to support his father's hand to remove it." "And he doubled, saying <b>I know, my son, I know</b> — he intended to respond to him regarding two things that he said, as we explained. Corresponding to what you said, ״No, my father, for this is the firstborn,״ and not as I thought, that they were arranged in reverse — ״I know, my son״; and he hinted by saying ״my son,״ meaning, and by implication you should not consider your right hand as prior to my right hand, nor should you arrange them [that way], but the firstborn [belongs] at my right hand and not at yours. And corresponding to what you instructed me to execute the law of the firstborn by your saying ״Put your right hand on his head״ — ״I know״ this too; and included in this knowledge is also knowledge of what results from this matter when doing thus to Joseph. And he said <b>he too shall become great</b> — meaning: do not consider that he is at a lowly level, but he shall become great and shall become a nation; <b>but</b> etc. — meaning: not on account of my blessing, but on account of what shall come from him — <b>and his seed shall be a multitude of nations.</b> Therefore, even though at this time this one is the firstborn, in the future the younger shall be greater, as they said, of blessed memory (Tanhuma), that from this one Gideon shall come forth and from that one Joshua shall come forth; and by implication this chain [of souls] was rooted in the root of the soul of the tribe even without Jacob's blessing, and therefore I am giving him precedence over the firstborn." "<b>Or</b> it may intend in this manner: I know all your claims, and what you hinted — that this one is the cause — it is not this one who is the cause, but rather my son, meaning, my son is the one who caused everything that transpires in your dreams and your words. And his saying <b>I know</b> a second time is drawn together with what follows it: ״he too, etc. but״ etc. — meaning: that he knew by prophecy that the younger would become greater than the older, and he was unable to do the reverse of the vision that the Master, blessed be He, had imaged in his hand."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:18.299780728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}